            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-45292",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "opentelemetry-java: opentelemetry-api: opentelemetry-extension-trace-propagators: OpenTelemetry Java: Denial of Service due to unbounded memory allocation when parsing oversized baggage"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "opentelemetry-java is the Java implementation of the OpenTelemetry API for recording telemetry, and SDK for managing telemetry recorded by the API. Prior to 1.62.0, a vulnerability affects the baggage propagation implementation in opentelemetry-api and opentelemetry-extension-trace-propagators. Parsing oversized baggage causes unbounded memory allocation and CPU consumption. Because baggage is automatically re-injected into every outgoing request, the effect can fan out to downstream services that never received the original malicious request. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.62.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45292",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-45292\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-api\nFixed Version: 1.62.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-45292](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45292)\nopentelemetry-java is the Java implementation of the OpenTelemetry API for recording telemetry, and SDK for managing telemetry recorded by the API. Prior to 1.62.0, a vulnerability affects the baggage propagation implementation in opentelemetry-api and opentelemetry-extension-trace-propagators. Parsing oversized baggage causes unbounded memory allocation and CPU consumption. Because baggage is automatically re-injected into every outgoing request, the effect can fan out to downstream services that never received the original malicious request. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.62.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-45292**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|io.opentelemetry:opentelemetry-api|1.62.0|[CVE-2026-45292](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45292)|\n\nopentelemetry-java is the Java implementation of the OpenTelemetry API for recording telemetry, and SDK for managing telemetry recorded by the API. Prior to 1.62.0, a vulnerability affects the baggage propagation implementation in opentelemetry-api and opentelemetry-extension-trace-propagators. Parsing oversized baggage causes unbounded memory allocation and CPU consumption. Because baggage is automatically re-injected into every outgoing request, the effect can fan out to downstream services that never received the original malicious request. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.62.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9689",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "keycloak: org.keycloak.protocol.oidc: HTTP Parameter Pollution in OIDC redirect URI allows response parameter duplication - #GHI-604"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in Keycloak, an open-source identity and access management solution. When a client application is configured to accept broad redirect Uniform Resource Identifiers (URIs), a remote attacker can manipulate the authentication process by crafting a special web address. If a user clicks this link, the client application might incorrectly prioritize attacker-controlled information over legitimate data. This vulnerability, known as HTTP parameter pollution, could allow an attacker to bypass security measures or gain unauthorized access to resources."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9689",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9689\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: org.keycloak:keycloak-services\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-9689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9689)\nA flaw was found in Keycloak, an open-source identity and access management solution. When a client application is configured to accept broad redirect Uniform Resource Identifiers (URIs), a remote attacker can manipulate the authentication process by crafting a special web address. If a user clicks this link, the client application might incorrectly prioritize attacker-controlled information over legitimate data. This vulnerability, known as HTTP parameter pollution, could allow an attacker to bypass security measures or gain unauthorized access to resources.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9689**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|org.keycloak:keycloak-services||[CVE-2026-9689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9689)|\n\nA flaw was found in Keycloak, an open-source identity and access management solution. When a client application is configured to accept broad redirect Uniform Resource Identifiers (URIs), a remote attacker can manipulate the authentication process by crafting a special web address. If a user clicks this link, the client application might incorrectly prioritize attacker-controlled information over legitimate data. This vulnerability, known as HTTP parameter pollution, could allow an attacker to bypass security measures or gain unauthorized access to resources."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 4.2,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "4.2",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9793",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "keycloak: Keycloak: Security policy bypass in JWE-encrypted request object processing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in Keycloak. When a JSON Web Encryption (JWE) encrypted request object is submitted, Keycloak may incorrectly process unsigned claims if the decrypted content is raw JSON, bypassing the configured signature policy. This allows a remote attacker to submit unauthorized claims, leading to a compromise of data integrity within the OpenID Connect (OIDC) authorization flow. While a redirect URI allowlist acts as a compensating control, this vulnerability violates OIDC Core and Financial-grade API (FAPI) signing requirements."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9793",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9793\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: org.keycloak:keycloak-services\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-9793](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9793)\nA flaw was found in Keycloak. When a JSON Web Encryption (JWE) encrypted request object is submitted, Keycloak may incorrectly process unsigned claims if the decrypted content is raw JSON, bypassing the configured signature policy. This allows a remote attacker to submit unauthorized claims, leading to a compromise of data integrity within the OpenID Connect (OIDC) authorization flow. While a redirect URI allowlist acts as a compensating control, this vulnerability violates OIDC Core and Financial-grade API (FAPI) signing requirements.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9793**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|org.keycloak:keycloak-services||[CVE-2026-9793](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9793)|\n\nA flaw was found in Keycloak. When a JSON Web Encryption (JWE) encrypted request object is submitted, Keycloak may incorrectly process unsigned claims if the decrypted content is raw JSON, bypassing the configured signature policy. This allows a remote attacker to submit unauthorized claims, leading to a compromise of data integrity within the OpenID Connect (OIDC) authorization flow. While a redirect URI allowlist acts as a compensating control, this vulnerability violates OIDC Core and Financial-grade API (FAPI) signing requirements."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.9,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.9",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-9798",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "keycloak: Keycloak: Brute-force protection bypass in CIBA flow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in Keycloak, an open-source identity and access management solution. When a user account is temporarily locked due to repeated failed login attempts, an attacker with valid client credentials can exploit the Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA) flow to bypass this brute-force protection. This allows continued authentication attempts and token issuance even when the account should be locked, potentially enabling further unauthorized access attempts."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9798",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-9798\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: org.keycloak:keycloak-services\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-9798](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9798)\nA flaw was found in Keycloak, an open-source identity and access management solution. When a user account is temporarily locked due to repeated failed login attempts, an attacker with valid client credentials can exploit the Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA) flow to bypass this brute-force protection. This allows continued authentication attempts and token issuance even when the account should be locked, potentially enabling further unauthorized access attempts.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-9798**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|org.keycloak:keycloak-services||[CVE-2026-9798](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9798)|\n\nA flaw was found in Keycloak, an open-source identity and access management solution. When a user account is temporarily locked due to repeated failed login attempts, an attacker with valid client credentials can exploit the Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA) flow to bypass this brute-force protection. This allows continued authentication attempts and token issuance even when the account should be locked, potentially enabling further unauthorized access attempts."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 4.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "4.3",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.71.2"
        }
